     Question

   The jump host server hosts a directory named /data, serving as a repository for various developers non-confidential data. Developer james has requested a copy of their data stored in /data/james. The System Admin team has provided the following steps to fulfill this request:
a. Create a compressed archive named james.tar.gz of the /data/james directory.
b. Transfer the archive to the /home directory on the Jump Host Server.

     Solution
1.Log in to the Jump Host Server
2.Create a compressed archive of /data/james
 Use tar with gzip compression:
  sudo tar -czf /tmp/james.tar.gz -C /data james
-c → create archive
-z → compress with gzip
-f → specify filename
-C /data james → ensures relative paths inside archive start from /data
This creates /tmp/james.tar.gz containing the entire james directory.
3.Transfer the archive to /home
  sudo mv /tmp/james.tar.gz /home/
4.Validate the archive
 Confirm file exists in /home:
  ls -lh /home/james.tar.gz

